WEBVTT

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:02.875
but that part of the team
that's over there in Belgium,

00:09:02.899 --> 00:09:05.740
they really don't work so hard,
they don't come in on time.

00:09:05.764 --> 00:09:07.418
We don't know what they're up to."

00:09:07.442 --> 00:09:12.706
So it's very easy to get those kind
of psychological distancing dynamics

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:13.885
that come into play,

00:09:13.909 --> 00:09:16.015
and it's a basic psychological process.

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.406
AG: In the study of airline crews,

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:21.576
the effective captains
created a shared identity.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.516
They talked about everyone as "we,"

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.116
not just the flight attendants,

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:27.666
but also the maintenance crew,
the gate agents

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.406
and even the air traffic controllers

00:09:29.430 --> 00:09:31.080
communicating remotely with them.